[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) is marked known: one issue, one fix queued. Its reports say otherwise.
They were merged on subject line alone ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)),
so three different bugs ended up in one ticket. One fix for the parser will close only the
first of them.

<Callout kind="warn">
Each problem below has its own ticket now. Link new reports to the ticket of their cause, not to #4471.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<ProblemTable
  ticket={4471}
  issues={{
    parser: 'https://github.com/johny7days/what-it-shows/issues/1',
    hint: 'https://github.com/johny7days/what-it-shows/issues/2',
    shift: 'https://github.com/johny7days/what-it-shows/issues/3',
  }}
/>

The table counts each report once (the export repeats some) and places it by its tenant and
the way it came in, as `#lib/kb/causes` does. The desk's one-day reading in `desk-notes.json`
takes a report out of `parser`. What intake tagged from the reporter's browser plays no part.

## The three problems

**`parser`: the shared parser reads day-first dates month first.** Every tenant in the
directory writes the day first. A booking for 7 April comes out as 4 July. In every
report the day is 12 or less. All channels.

**`hint`: booking-v3 tells people to type MM/DD.** Only through the form, only for tenants on
booking-v3. People do what the hint says and type the month first; the form reads the date
the tenant's way, day first. The dates flip like `parser`, but the fix is the form's hint, not
the parser. A parser fix alone leaves these reports open.

**`shift`: the invite moves by one day.** No month flips here. Tuesday 12 May shows as
Monday 11 May; a client in Lisbon got Tuesday while a client in Toronto got Monday for the
same meeting; one invite arrived before the booking was made. The reports do not say why;
time zones or daylight saving are a guess. It is not date order, so a parser fix will not
touch it.

## Against the desk's own table

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

The desk's table already sees `hint` as not belonging to #4471. It still counts the one-day
moves inside `parser` and only footnotes them.

## For the desk

- Merge by cause, not by subject: the same subject covers all three problems.
- Keep #4471 for `parser` only, or close it in favour of its ticket.
- Re-run this page after the next export: every number here is computed.

